# gen_fu_l42_dbg_dret_entry.log -- TDD red/green and MUT-MEPCSKEW1 for the dret-target rule
# Produced 2026-09-05T05:14:04Z on soc-l-11 from a detached archive of 27212cb with this
# landing's file applied.
#
# THE DEFECT, measured before it was fixed: dbg_dret required the record after a dret to be at dpc and
# exempted only a debug re-entry, so an interrupt taken at the dret target was called a mismatch. That entry
# is the coverage plan's own cp_post_exit.taken_before_first_insn case, so the checker forbade a case the plan
# expects to cover. It was unreachable in round 1, which took zero interrupt entries.
#
# THE FIXTURE: gen_ut_dbg on the directed interrupt program under a storm irq regime, which is the only shape
# in the tree today that puts a pending line and a debug session in the same run.
#   image dv/auto_dv/stim/gen_directed/gen_irq_directed.S, 156 words, crc32 0x8e882c5b, tohost 0x800002d0
#   plusargs: +gen_fetch_en_at_reset=0 +gen_knob_irq_regime=storm
# THE ARITHMETIC that says the flagged record is a legitimate entry and not a wrong target: gen_vec is at
# 0x80000200 in that image and the vectored entry for cause 17 (fast[1]) is 0x80000200 + 4*17 = 0x80000244,
# which is the pc the committed checker flagged. The run compared 460 records with ZERO ISA mismatches, so
# the model produced the same record.
#
# BUILDS (dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_tb_local.sh compile), differing only as stated:
#   outRed  gen_checkers_pkg.sv exactly as committed at 27212cb
#   outFix  with the fix
#   outMut  the fix, plus MUT-MEPCSKEW1 in gen_rvfi_pkg.sv
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

