#   file:line: dv/auto_dv/env/gen_rvfi_pkg.sv, publish_state's mepc read
#   original: st.mepc = gen_isa_read_csr(ibex_pkg::CSR_MEPC);
#   mutated:  st.mepc = gen_isa_read_csr(ibex_pkg::CSR_MEPC) + 32'd4;
#   expected detector: the dbg_dret rule's NEW positive check, that an entry at the dret target carries
#     mepc == dpc; the message names both values
#   caught: outMut/mut_named, one UVM_ERROR, mepc 80000122 against dpc 8000011e, which is the skew exactly
#   ablation control: outMut/mut_ablated, the same build and fixture with the named check not enabled:
#     zero UVM_ERRORs, so the mutation survives and the verdict belongs to the named check alone
#   The mutation proves the fix is not merely an exemption: a wrong-target entry still fails.
#   READ THE ABLATION'S COUNTER CAREFULLY: its report line still says failures=1. The rule DETECTED the
#   mutation and did not REPORT it, because gen_chk_en gates only the uvm_error and not the counting. That is
#   what an ablation is meant to show, and the run's verdict is PASS with zero UVM_ERRORs.
